      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under GDPR, \"right to be forgotten\" requests extend to all personal data, including archived backups, meaning companies must actively identify and remove this residual data where technically feasible to comply with the law. However, if erasing data from deep historical archives requires disproportionate effort or renders the backups unusable for legitimate legal proceedings, organizations may apply for a derogation (exception) based on Article 23 to allow retained processing instead of deletion. It is crucial for your memo to emphasize that while the legal expectation is comprehensive deletion, practical limitations must be weighed against the obligation of transparency, often requiring a case-by-case legal review in such edge cases.",
